e because I don't you know people  would argue against gay marriage saying  it's unnatural I disagreed I mean  homosexuality exists and who knows how  many thousand species I disagreed with  the unnatural argument but I also  thought that it was a bad argument  whether things are or aren't quote  natural however it's defined that's not  a good enough reason for me to decide  something should or shouldn't be illegal  or accepted in society so number one is  that this equality of outcome doesn't  happen doesn't occur naturally in the  world but that in and of itself is not a  good enough reason to say we shouldn't  be for equality of outcome let's  actually ask the question would equality  of outcome be good in society and the  answer is what kind right  what kind if we're talking about an  inequality of outcome where the poor and  middle class do much much better we  raised the bottom and we reduce the  difference between the top and the  bottom and we use whatever economic  mechanism that we determine is the right  one to increase well-being then you can  have some inequality and that's okay if  you're saying we need equality of  outcome in that everybody gets their  shot at being senator or something like  that that's not an equality of outcome  that I would get behind so just saying  equality of outcome good bad indifferent  we need to know what we're talking about  we need to understand how it is that  that equality would be achieved and then  we can figure out does equality of  outcome makes sense or not and what I  think we would quickly realize is that  in many endeavors in life equality of  outcome wouldn't actually even be the  right target but I want to go back to  where I started very few people are  actually calling for total equality of  outcome in the economy in other  endeavors and to pretend as though  there's this big equality of outcome  movement is fundamentally deceptive
 

